{"parentUuid":"fdefa25d-d10e-4876-ab3d-7c9f6766ba4a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLX8qD24w7gGq8BFZSuP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling is moot: 0.14.1 had already published when I checked, so there was nothing left to stop.\n\n- **0.14.1 is out:** it is on crates.io and the GitHub release is marked Latest. It includes the tag hints (written and read) and the two changelog entries about them.\n- **Impact:** low. Tags made by 0.14.1 carry about 130 bytes of extra annotation, and readers fall back without it. Nothing breaks.\n- **Fix:** release PR #345 is already open. It will ship #341 (look patience), #342 (hints removed) and #343 (cleanup) as 0.14.2. You'll want to check its changelog says plainly that the hints were removed and are not just silently absent.\n- **Changelog:** I'd leave the 0.14.1 entries as they are. They are an accurate record of what that release did.\n- **Remaining risk:** if you cut a release from 0.14.1's binary before 0.14.2, its tags carry hints. Nothing reads them after #342, so they are inert.\n\nMerge #345 when its CI is green, re-triggering CI first since the workflow token won't. I won't touch it.\n\nMy mistake was not telling you to hold #340 earlier. I raised the order only after it had merged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":441499,"output_tokens":408,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":441499,"cache_creation_input_tokens":597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":597},"type":"message"}