 or network commands.\n\n## Findings\n\n| criterion id | what the spec says | what is true now | evidence | proposed corrected wording |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| REL-CMD-08 (also api_surface \"Invalid --package: E227, E102 or E169\") | E169 is listed for \"a duplicate selection, a version whose release is complete, or a package with no publish target\". | Incomplete. E169 is also raised for any selected package whose version is a `callisto snapshot` version (`0.0.0-snapshot…` or `0.0.0.dev0+…`). This applies to every release, with or without `--package`, and nothing in the spec mentions it. | `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/derive.rs`, `build_publish_leaves`, returns `ReleaseSelectionInvalid{SnapshotVersion}` for every selected package. `snapshot.rs:165` defines `is_snapshot_version`. `docs/errors.md:211` documents the E169 case. | \"A malformed `--package` value fails with `E227` and an unknown package with E102. A duplicate selection, a version whose release is complete, a package with no publish target, or a package whose current version is a `callisto snapshot` version fails with E169.\" |\n| REL-CMD-04 | \"a table on a colour terminal, `Release plan:` lines otherwise\". | Partly imprecise. The `Release plan:` header is printed in both modes. On a colour terminal the table follows it. Otherwise each package is an indented `<ecosystem/name> <version>` line with `- <operation>` lines under it. | `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs`, `render_release_plan`. Binary output without a colour terminal: `Release plan:` then `  cargo/foo 0.1.0` then `    - publish to crates.io` and `    - create git tag`. | \"…prints a `Release plan:` header followed by each package as `<ecosystem/name> <version>` with its operations (a table on a colour terminal, indented lines otherwise)…\" |\n| REL-PUB-11 (minor) | Masks \"the values of … any variable named `*_TOKEN`, `*_SECRET` or `*_PASSWORD`\". | A variable matching those suffixes is masked only when its value is at least 8 characters. `CARGO_REGISTRIES_*_TOKEN` is also masked. | `crates/callisto-model/src/registry.rs:247-257`, where `MIN_SECRET_VALUE_LEN = 8`. | \"…the values of the known credential variables, of `CARGO_REGISTRIES_*_TOKEN`, and of any variable named `*_TOKEN`, `*_SECRET` or `*_PASSWORD` whose value is at least 8 characters…\" |\n\n## Checked and confirmed\n- **Error codes:** every code the spec cites exists in `docs/errors.md` and in the code with the meaning the spec gives. I checked E025, E059, E102, E104, E120, E124–E126, E132, E139–E154, E157, E163–E167, E169, E170, E172, E175, E176, E179, E180, E197, E198, E215–E219, E221, E227, E230–E233, E239, E266, E267, E281, E306–E309, E318, E320 and E321.\n- **Schema versions:** intent is 5 (`intent.rs:98`), decision is 2 with 1 and 2 readable (`decision.rs:118-120`), run envelope is 3 and receipt is 2.\n- **Subcommands and flags:** the hidden subcommands exist with the flags the spec names (`crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs`). `build-python`, `--seal-python` and `inspect` are present. `--emit-decision`, `--refresh-lockfiles` and `--no-refresh-lockfiles` exist.\n- **Timing:**\n  - Looks are 15 s, 45 s, 2 min, then 3 min steps (`policy.rs` `visibility_backoff`).\n  - Default windows are 360 s for npm and PyPI and 120 s otherwise (`policy.rs:63-69`).\n  - A look's own retries are clamped to the time left in the window (`release_execution.rs` `settle_issued`).\n  - The window opens at the first issue and persists across looks (`ConfirmationWave`).\n  - `publish-timeout` defaults to 900 s (`policy.rs:18`), and `confirm-timeout` and `publish-timeout` accept 1 s to 1 h (`config/duration.rs`).\n  - Observation retries make 5 attempts with 2/4/8/16 s waits and a 300 s cap.\n  - GitHub effect visibility makes 6 attempts with 2/4/8/16/32 s waits (`policy.rs:141-157`).\n- **Operation ordering:**\n  - Dependency edges are runtime, build, optional and dev, with a dev edge inside a cycle ignored (`toposort.rs` `PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS`).\n  - Only npm defers confirmation (`registry.rs:234`, `NpmRegistry::defers_confirmation`).\n  - A registry publish may follow an issued registry publish; everything else needs a confirmed prerequisite (`release_execution.rs` `eligible_in`).\n  - The tag waits for the registry publishes of every manifest of its package, and the draft waits for the tag.\n  - The product's publish waits for the uploads and for the tag of any other asset-owning package (`derive.rs`).\n  - Platform publishes use `npm publish <dir>` and run before the owner publish.\n- **Publish tooling:**\n  - Cargo, npm, pnpm, yarn and bun argv, the dist-tag rule (`derive.rs` `npm_dist_tag`), the scoped-package default `--access public`, and the PyPI build argv with `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` match `registry_argv.rs`.\n  - The `cargo info`, `npm view` and PyPI simple-index observations match `registry.rs`.\n  - The `release create` argv matches `forge.rs`.\n  - The tag message is `Release <tag>` (`derive.rs:593`) and tags are created unsigned.\n- **Release PR:**\n  - The action scripts and `action.yml` match: `.callisto/release-decision.json` default, staging branch reset, `createCommitOnBranch`, no `git push`, verify before commit, before ref move, and before label or PR write.\n  - The final check retries 9 times with 3 s sleeps, which is 27 s.\n  - Mode validation, `run-release.sh` and `install-callisto.sh` also match.\n- **Release workflow:**\n  - `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` appears only on the execute step, and top-level `permissions: {}`.\n  - Recovery gating by `recovery-checks`, the 40-lowercase-hex check, and the verified-merge and managed-branch checks match `callisto-release.yml`.\n  - There is no Environment or reviewer gate.\n- **Local config rules:**\n  - The release roster, group expansion and `require_dependencies_selected` (runtime, optional, peer) match.\n  - The legacy `[release.profiles.production]` handling matches ERR-03.\n- **Binary runs on a scratch repo under `/tmp/claude-501/spdrift-rel`:**\n  - `release --dry-run` prints the plan and the origin note.\n  - `release` without an origin fails with E132.\n  - `release` on an untracked file fails with E267 naming the path.\n  - `--package foo` fails with E227, `cargo/nope` with E102, and a duplicate with E169.\n  - JSON dry-run has `schemaVersion` 5, `digest`, `command: release` and `dryRun: true`.\n  - `release-pr decide` produced E141, E142, E143, E144, E145, E147 and E154 as specified.\n  - `release-pr verify` accepts the decorated decide output as a file, on stdin and inline.\n  - `verify` returns E148 on a changed snapshot and E281 for a bad `dryRun` and for an unknown field.\n  - `--dry-run` with `release artifact-manifest`, `execute` and `build-python` gives E216, E218 and E309.\n  - `release plan --from-release-commit abc` fails with E224. `release plan --package` on a dirty tree fails with E267. The spec does not name these codes.\n\n## Not verified (code read only, or needs a network or real registry)\n- Live behaviour of npm, cargo, twine and `gh`, including `gh attestation verify` flags in a real run (the flags are in `release_artifacts.rs:212-234`).\n- REL-RERUN-07 / E320: the version-commit first-parent walk and content comparison (`release/version_commit.rs`) were not exercised.\n- REL-PUB-08 PyPI E307 digest matching, sealed-file handling and the yanked-file conflict path.\n- REL-PUB-14: the foreign-repository warning's host, owner and name normalisation.\n- REL-AUTH-09: that execution rejects artifact slots targeting another repository.\n- REL-AUTH-07: the E267 mapping for a worktree that goes dirty mid-run.\n- REL-PR-03: the over-4 MiB (E152), mode (E150) and path (E153) rules were not exercised. Only the 4 MiB constant (`release_pr.rs:519`) was seen. E149 on `commit-plan` was not reachable (a bad base commit gave E051).\n- REL-PR-06: the pinned-ref resolution against real tags.\n- `.github/tests/*` and `just workflow-contracts`, which I did not run.\n\n## Housekeeping\nMy first scratch repo was at `/tmp/claude-501/sd`, which another agent was also using. I ran `rm -rf` on it before noticing, so that agent's scratch may be gone. My scratch repo is now `/tmp/claude-501/spdrift-rel`, and helper scripts are `/tmp/claude-501/{sd-setup,cal,rp,rp2}.sh`."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":181,"turnIndex":322},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/spec-drift","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
