{"parentUuid":"1cce899a-579f-4abd-a407-be95c06b8b88","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLam7dr7pUz6H7zwXNmi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the list in order, with the first three being the ones I'd treat as blockers.\n\n**1. A real end-to-end run on real registries.** This is the biggest gap.\n- Everything is verified against fakes, scratch registries and my own binary runs. Cargo and PyPI tests drive the publisher directly and skip registry binding, and nothing has run on real registries with hosted GitHub.\n- The \"under ten minutes from a fresh repo to a first release\" goal has never been measured.\n- This needs your credentials and a throwaway package set. I can write the script, but you'd have to run it.\n\n**2. Pin the one-way doors.** These can't change after 1.0 without a major bump:\n- tag format, report and decision `schemaVersion` meanings, `callisto.toml` keys (it rejects unknown keys and has no schema version), the decision file path, the npm dist-tag policy, error-code stability, and action inputs.\n- None of these is written down as a promise. A short \"stability\" page in the docs would do it. This is mostly writing, plus a few decisions from you.\n\n**3. Your open decisions.**\n- Accept ADR 12.\n- OIDC for npm: currently a long-lived `NPM_TOKEN` of a type npm is deprecating.\n- How a private workspace root is excluded.\n- Whether a fixed group can share one tag or release title (today it can't).\n- Private and HTML-only PyPI indexes.\n\n**4. Two known gaps.**\n- A private root `package.json` is listed as a package (`npm/monorepo`).\n- A fixed group has one release title per package.\n- I haven't re-checked the `#290` guard's history-cap and merge-only-edit gaps since the later fix.\n\n**5. Small cleanup.**\n- Flip the \"pre-v1\" wording in README and SECURITY.\n- Fix the `macos-13` runner and the missing platforms in `proto/callisto.toml`.\n- Enable immutable releases and decide the Entire push setting.\n- Document the manual first publish on crates.io and npm.\n\n**What I would not do:** more performance work, `cargo-semver-checks` (the library crates are documented internal), or the michi edge-kind refactor.\n\nIf you want one thing to start, I'd write the stability page (item 2) and the real-registry run script (item 1), since both are blocked only on things I can prepare. Should I start there?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":488270,"output_tokens":1223,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":452},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1223,"cache_read_input_tokens":488270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b568a70a-2b68-449a-afa8-368d4f93a664","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgLam79KaSKJZjYLbRnsv","requestRef":"24c466e5-918b-4c7d-9803-66475e11b787","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9be061e-2d4d-4943-b053-13bfc9448445","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:24:04.179Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/spec-drift","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
