{"parentUuid":"18ff3e54-b763-4a02-8010-f6917e773834","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17e5e12e-3a39-45c3-bf9e-35421bdea6f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0161yDdnWCsRd6tEJDAkS5M3","type":"tool_result","content":"name=\ntag=callisto@0.14.1\n---\n- Release tags now record the package that made them and the git tree of each of its directories in the tag message, as Callisto-Package and Callisto-Tree lines. Nothing reads them yet, and tags without them keep working.\n- Waiting for npm packages to appear is now one window of confirm-timeout for the whole release: a package that shows up along the way no longer restarts it, and the time spent checking the registry counts, so a slow registry cannot stretch the wait to several windows.\n- `status`, `version` and `release` skip two history reads for tags made by a recent release. They still read them for every other tag, so older and hand-made tags behave as before.\n40 matches in 1 files:\n\n15:confirmed_evidence, wrong_role, EffectAuthorization, ForgePublishOperation, F...\n16:PreparedOperation, ProviderCapabilities, ProviderContext, ProviderRequest, Re...\n58:let notes_dir;\n59:let notes_file = match &operation.notes {\n60:ReleaseNotes::Section(section) => {\n61:notes_dir = tempfile::tempdir().map_err(notes_file_error)?;\n62:let path = notes_dir.path().join(\"notes.md\");\n63:callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write(&path, section, effect.permit).map_err(n...\n66:ReleaseNotes::Generated { reason } => {\n67:eprintln!(\"{}\", generated_notes_notice(&request.id.package, *reason));\n71:let create_args = release_create_args(operation, &repository, notes_file.as_d...\n89:/// `gh release create` for a draft: the changelog section when `notes_file` ...\n93:notes_file: Option<&'a str>,\n104:match notes_file {\n105:Some(path) => args.extend([\"--notes-file\", path]),\n106:None => args.push(\"--generate-notes\"),\n114:fn generated_notes_notice(package: &ReleasePackageId, reason: NotesFallback) ...\n115:format!(\"notes: using generated notes ({reason}) for {package}\")\n118:fn notes_file_error(error: std::io::Error) -> GraphError {\n120:path: \"notes.md\".into(),\n469:fn forge_operation_with(notes: ReleaseNotes) -> ForgeReleaseOperation {\n473:notes,\n477:/// A changelog section is passed as `--notes-file`, never with `--generate-n...\n479:fn changelog_section_is_passed_as_a_notes_file() {\n480:let operation = forge_operation_with(ReleaseNotes::Section(\"- fix\".to_owned()));\n  +15 more in crates/.../provider/forge.rs [see remaining: tail -n +26 \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1792823197_grep_0_m_6cd1c0.log\"]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5f77052d-5033-42f2-89bb-471961baad6f","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:26:38.037Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"name=\ntag=callisto@0.14.1\n---\n- Release tags now record the package that made them and the git tree of each of its directories in the tag message, as Callisto-Package and Callisto-Tree lines. Nothing reads them yet, and tags without them keep working.\n- Waiting for npm packages to appear is now one window of confirm-timeout for the whole release: a package that shows up along the way no longer restarts it, and the time spent checking the registry counts, so a slow registry cannot stretch the wait to several windows.\n- `status`, `version` and `release` skip two history reads for tags made by a recent release. They still read them for every other tag, so older and hand-made tags behave as before.\n40 matches in 1 files:\n\n15:confirmed_evidence, wrong_role, EffectAuthorization, ForgePublishOperation, F...\n16:PreparedOperation, ProviderCapabilities, ProviderContext, ProviderRequest, Re...\n58:let notes_dir;\n59:let notes_file = match &operation.notes {\n60:ReleaseNotes::Section(section) => {\n61:notes_dir = tempfile::tempdir().map_err(notes_file_error)?;\n62:let path = notes_dir.path().join(\"notes.md\");\n63:callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write(&path, section, effect.permit).map_err(n...\n66:ReleaseNotes: