{"parentUuid":"29413310-40e8-47cf-b2c2-3b33a2d0b592","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLb2WUh4cyg8U5GMqCCd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1578,"cache_read_input_tokens":498390,"output_tokens":1894,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1356},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1578,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1894,"cache_read_input_tokens":498390,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1578},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":16524,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"5a212657-0568-496b-a20b-88e6e3b7554d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgLb2W6NCgwX4n4TN5Lw3","requestRef":"7d5d7470-085d-409b-9420-7e7dfa1881c7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c610f5fe-4606-4f8a-8acf-ef4bd7373c16","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:27:40.014Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/spec-drift","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c610f5fe-4606-4f8a-8acf-ef4bd7373c16","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLb2WUh4cyg8U5GMqCCd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: it's a real bug, and I can reproduce it.\n\n**What happens**\n- A GitHub release takes its notes from only the release-owning package's changelog section.\n- In a fixed group, a member gets only its own changesets plus boilerplate such as \"Released together with the `lockstep` fixed group.\"\n- So if a changeset names `cargo/b` and the release owner is `cargo/a`, `a`'s changelog and its GitHub release say nothing about `b`'s feature.\n- I reproduced this in a scratch repo. After `version`, `a/CHANGELOG.md` read only \"Released together with the `lockstep` group\", while the real change sat in `b/CHANGELOG.md`.\n- This is why Callisto's own releases look fine: every changeset names `callisto-cli`, which owns the release. Any group whose changes land on a non-owner member gets empty-looking notes.\n\n**Where the fix goes (my recommendation)**\n- Keep the changelog files as they are.\n- Build the GitHub release notes for a fixed-group package from the union of all members' sections for that version. Drop the boilerplate lines, remove duplicates, and prefix an entry with its package when it came from another member.\n- The alternative is to copy every member's entries into each member's own changelog. That is simpler but noisy, because it repeats the same entry in every crate's changelog.\n\n**Not covered**\n- The untitled release name, which is the separate fixed-group tag and title gap from michi's feedback. It would need its own design.\n\nShall I go with the release-notes union? It's a contained change in `notes.rs` and `derive.rs`, with a test using the repro above."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1578,"cache_read_input_tokens":498