{"parentUuid":"91f55936-f12c-42e0-a7aa-dcdecd958734","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLbv6RHYvWAyaXrzdjaD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015HPuQ6rj8meHJFaR1YnswF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr view 348 --json body --jq .body | head -8","description":"Read the body PR 348 was created with","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":528645,"output_tokens":620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":528645,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015HPuQ6rj8meHJFaR1YnswF":{"command":"gh pr view 348 --json body --jq .body | head -8","description":"Read the body PR 348 was created with","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b954bfb9-ad75-454c-b4ba-e905a0a1ef4a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgLbv5zzMf91jSJpvhyPH","requestRef":"8f641720-9fab-461d-8765-a48d7661e2ab","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7a8c1a8-22b6-4888-84a4-8024a42ab099","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:39:04.988Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c7a8c1a8-22b6-4888-84a4-8024a42ab099","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLbv6RHYvWAyaXrzdjaD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KYof9Q3PfwqCdAzviBoRJb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_targets_final.md","content":"Two release-target facts were out of date now that Intel macOS and arm64 Linux binaries are published.\n\n- The generated build matrix mapped `x86_64-apple-darwin` to `macos-13`, a runner GitHub has retired, so a job on it would never get a machine. It now uses `macos-latest` like the Apple Silicon triple; a Rust target builds on either architecture with `--target`. The matrix test and the matrix spec follow.\n- `proto/callisto.toml` listed only macOS arm64 and Linux x64, so proto users on Intel macOS or arm64 Linux could not install a binary that exists. It now lists `x86_64` for macOS and `aarch64` for Linux. An arm64 musl build is not published, so arm64 Alpine is still unsupported.\n\n`just ci` passes. Not exercised: a real proto install on those platforms.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":528645,"output_tokens":620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":528645,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KYof9Q3PfwqCdAzviBoRJb":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_targets_final.md","content":"Two release-target facts were out of date now that Intel macOS and arm64 Linux binaries are published.\n\n- The generated build matrix mapped `x86_64-apple-darwin` to `macos-13`, a runner GitHub has retired, so a job on it would never get a machine. It now uses `macos-latest` like the Apple Silicon triple; a Rust target builds on either architecture with `--target`. The matrix test and the matrix spec follow.\n- `proto/callisto.toml` listed only macOS arm64 and Linux x64, so proto users on Intel macOS or arm64 Linux could not install a binary that exists. It now lists `x86_64` for macOS and `aarch64` for Linux. An arm64 musl build is not published, so arm64 Alpine is still unsupported.\n\n`just ci` passes. Not exercised: a real proto install on those platforms.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b954bfb9-ad75-454c-b4ba-e905a0a1ef4a","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgLbv5zzMf91jSJpvhyPH","requestRef":"8f641720-9fab-461d-8765-a48d7661e2ab","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"df301f1a-f013-4a04-93a1-a89fea285781","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:39:06.497Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c7a8c1a8-22b6-4888-84a4-8024a42ab099","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"611a0958-8088-4957-ad50-7eed36897c7a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015HPuQ6rj8meHJFaR1YnswF","type":"tool_result","content":"Callisto's release binaries covered Apple silicon macOS, x86_64 Linux (gnu and musl) only. Intel Macs and arm64 Linux machines, including arm64 CI runners, built from crates.io instead. This adds both:\n\n- `x86_64-apple-darwin`, cross-compiled on the Apple silicon runner (`macos-14`) with the same `cargo build --target` recipe as the existing macOS asset.\n- `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, built natively on the `ubuntu-24.04-arm` runner. glibc 2.39 is required, as it already is for the x86_64 gnu asset.\n\nChanged together, because they have to agree: the two `[[release.artifact]]` entries in `callisto.toml`, the release workflow's build matrix, the CI preflight matrix (so a broken recipe fails before a release), the build script's allowlist, and the `setup-callisto` installer, which now maps `Darwin x86_64` and `Linux aarch64`/`arm64` to their assets. The release workflow policy check already cross-checks these lists and passes.\n\nThe installer is safe for pinned older releases: they have no such asset, the download fails, and it falls back to crates.io exactly as an unsupported machine does today. New installer tests cover every platform's asset name and an unsupported architecture.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f62112a6-1501-4281-aceb-9e93e302b900","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:39:08.648Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Callisto's release binaries covered Apple silicon macOS, x86_64 Linux (gnu and musl) only. Intel Macs and arm64 Linux machines, including arm64 CI runners, built from crates.io instead. This adds both:\n\n- `x86_64-apple-darwin`, cross-compiled on the Apple silicon runner (`macos-14`) with the same `cargo build --target` recipe as the existing macOS asset.\n- `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, built natively on the `ubuntu-24.04-arm` runner. glibc 2.39 is required, as it already is for the x86_64 gnu asset.\n\nChanged together, because they have to agree: the two `[[release.artifact]]` entries in `callisto.toml`, the release workflow's build matrix, the CI preflight matrix (so a broken recipe fails before a release), the build script's allowlist, and the `setup-callisto` installer, which now maps `Darwin x86_64` and `Linux aarch64`/`arm64` to their assets. The release workflow policy check already cross-checks these lists and passes.\n\nThe installer is safe for pinned older releases: they have no such asset, the download fails, and it falls back to crates.io exactly as an unsupported machine does today. New installer tests cover every platform's asset name and an unsupported architecture.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b954bfb9-ad75-454c-b4ba-e905a0a1ef4a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c7a8c1a8-22b6-4888-84a4-8024a42ab099","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
