 tool teams can trust to publish to public registries from CI without leaking secrets, publishing the wrong thing, or being tricked by untrusted input.\n\nRULES: read-only. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network publishes. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-security-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never use a shared path, never rm outside your own dir). Never run git commands in the real repo except read-only `git log/show`.\n\nYOUR LENS: security and trust boundaries. Attack it: (1) the GitHub workflow/action design (.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml, .github/actions/*, scripts under .github/): untrusted PR content reaching a privileged job, expression/shell injection through branch names/PR titles/changeset text/package names/versions, artifact download trust between jobs, what `execute` trusts, token scopes, pull_request_target-style hazards, actions pinning; (2) the release intent/decision/receipt digest chain: what is bound and what is NOT (e.g. things outside the digest that influence effects: registry endpoints, publish args, notes, tag annotation), TOCTOU between plan and execute, replay of an old intent, a malicious committed decision file; (3) path containment and symlink handling in manifest/changelog/artifact paths, archive extraction, `..` in config paths (changelog, package dirs, artifact dirs); (4) command construction for cargo/npm/pnpm/twine/gh/git: argument injection from package names, versions, tags, registry URLs, dist-tags; env var leakage into child processes; credential redaction gaps (output, errors, JSON, receipts, logs); (5) supply chain of Callisto itself: the installer (.github/actions/setup-callisto, scripts), checksum/attestation verification, floating tags.\nFor each finding give: severity (critical/high/medium/low), exact file:line, a concrete attack or failure scenario, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop anything speculative that you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things that are done WELL (so the owner knows what not to touch). Be concise and precise.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/tasks/a09833c9f278a9ab6.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10d5f8d8-491b-4598-ad2c-cfbc872079f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d634190-3821-4450-91f5-6fdf340df748","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
