E.md and all ADRs (1-12), docs/architecture/*.md, docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, docs/how-callisto-works.md, then skim the crate layout (crates/callisto-model, -manifests, -graph, -cli, -fixtures) and the public API surface.\n\nRULES: read-only. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto (--help, init, status, version --dry-run, release --dry-run) on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-arch-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never share paths; never rm outside your own dir).\n\nProduct goal (derive it from the docs, then challenge it): a trustworthy, fast, low-ceremony release tool for polyglot monorepos that is changesets-compatible, makes the committed decision the release authority, observes registries to recover from failure, and needs under ten minutes to a first release.\nYOUR LENS: does the design serve that goal, and where will it hurt at 1.0 and beyond? Challenge: (1) the identity model (directory-keyed packages, display-id promotion, canonical `ecosystem/name`, release ownership for dual packages, tag naming) — which cases still produce surprising behavior or one-way-door mistakes?; (2) the 1.0 contracts that cannot change later (tag format, report/decision/intent schemaVersions, config keys, error codes, action inputs, exit codes, hidden commands the CI route depends on): which are under-specified, leaky, or accidentally public?; (3) complexity budget: where is the codebase doing too much (size of modules, duplicated logic, abstraction layers that do not pay for themselves, features nobody asked for), and what could be deleted?; (4) onboarding and day-2 operations: what does a new user hit in the first hour (init, workflow generation, secrets, first publish bootstrap on crates.io/npm/PyPI), and what does a maintainer hit when a release half-fails; error message quality (run real failing commands and judge them); (5) extensibility claims vs reality (adding Go/NuGet, a new registry, a new forge such as GitLab); (6) competitor fit: what would make a team choose changesets/release-plz/cargo-dist/semantic-release/Nx release instead, honestly.\nFor each finding give: severity (blocks-1.0 / should-fix / consider), evidence (file:line or command output), the concrete harm, and a one-line recommendation. Rank. At most 12 findings; no speculation without evidence. Also list 3-5 design decisions that are RIGHT and should be defended. Be concise and direct, a principal engineer's voice.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/tasks/a90597a92b6fe2c68.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10d5f8d8-491b-4598-ad2c-cfbc872079f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9eab9565-d663-4d08-810c-27f598f68cc6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c