{"parentUuid":"76a585d0-4326-46c8-97de-f131697fe92e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMQf8Zpi9AfJCjENdeRT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The adversarial review is running as five read-only investigations; none has reported yet. Each reproduces what it can on scratch repos and ranks its top findings with file and line.\n\n- **Security and trust boundaries:** workflow and action injection, what the intent digest does and doesn't bind, path containment, command construction, secret redaction, and Callisto's own supply chain.\n- **Failure and recovery:** crash windows around each registry, tag and GitHub effect, overlapping runs, lost responses, and the version-commit and confirmation-window logic.\n- **Versioning correctness:** manifest and lockfile edits on unusual inputs, semver and PEP 440 handling, cascade cycles, pre mode, changeset parsing and half-written trees.\n- **Architecture and product fit:** the identity model, the one-way contracts for 1.0, what to delete, the first-hour and day-2 experience, and an honest comparison with the alternatives.\n- **Test assurance:** where fakes diverge from real tools, which important behaviors have no failing-case test, rubber-stamp snapshots, and CI jobs that can pass while testing nothing.\n\nWhen they finish I'll check the strongest findings myself before I report anything, since agent findings are leads, not conclusions. I'll then give you one ranked list with what I confirmed, what I couldn't, and what to do first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8882,"cache_read_input_tokens":532143,"output_tokens":441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8882,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":532143,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8882},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"20d0f1e7-9843-4ecd-bb67-e73b7aedbc64","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMQf87ntAFRXL4hwZGGr","requestRef":"29dd2de2-c235-4cd1-b059-7b7ba1261845","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c8e05998-1e77-4838-95c0-5c8bded48102","timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:52:05.724Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
