{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","id":"bdb24e65-a586-4e2a-8131-30151a94509f","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:40:49.786Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"761156c7f8e5f9beaaf03c55d45c00e6108ed5cc90a785040747ceaf99aae387","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"ba41e5ec-d55d-45f6-a14b-6bde3852637b","keep":917,"tail":["f43de78a32c2cd34397dd2d6fcdd1d6cf59a01100aedb9d459e879ac1e3b10c0","ae16fd15fdab51b9949054be30eb93178164f9f30c1256fd848d02218a0d7531","9eb9742c001bef03fa50969113d73d4fa992901e78affebd7719b233762a6037"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",919,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f729219be236a2beb20d15508a0c1def189954ea478adaa256f219eaa40b4c93"}
{"parentUuid":"60a35dd1-0ed2-4df6-98b4-f84adc5f7c4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUP75oFg3dN75fvoWvs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. With agents the coding is cheap, so the limit is your decisions and calendar time, and legacy removal should happen first. Here is what to remove and what to keep, so we don't cut something we're about to add back.\n\n**Remove now (dead, and nothing coming back)**\n\n| Item | State today | Plan |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[init]` table | \"Deprecated; parsed for compatibility, never read\" | Delete. A config that still has it gets a clear error, not a silent ignore. |\n| `[release.profiles]` | Only `profiles.production` is read, once, to migrate `forge-repository` | Delete. The migration was for early adopters, so give it one release of an error that names the new key. |\n| `setup_git_user` action input | A documented no-op | Delete. |\n| `cargo install --git main` installer fallback | Runs unreleased code with credentials | Delete. |\n\n**Keep (the replacement is imminent, or it isn't a promise)**\n- **`id-token: write` in generated workflows.** I had suggested dropping it because nothing uses it yet. OIDC for npm is next, so we'd add it right back; keep it.\n- **The `Ecosystem` enum variants** (Go, Maven, NuGet, Deno, Jsr). The enum is non-exhaustive and internal, so it isn't a user promise, and keeping it costs nothing.\n- **Config keys that do something today** (`confirm-timeout`, `publish-timeout`, `previous-tag-templates`).\n\n**Your call**\n- **`publish-to = \"nuget\"`.** It's accepted but no publisher exists, so a user can configure something that silently does nothing. If a NuGet publisher is more than a few weeks out, reject it with a clear \"not supported yet\" message and add it back with the publisher. If it's close, keep it and say it's unsupported. I'd reject it.\n\n**The timeline.** With agents, items 1–8 are about a day or two of work, and the cheap follow-ups another couple of days. The calendar risk isn't coding, it's:\n\n1. **Your decisions.** Tag naming, ADR 12, skipping non-publishable members, nuget, and OIDC.\n2. **Anything needing your credentials.** The real-registry end-to-end run is the largest unverified thing, and only you can start it.\n3. **Elapsed time.** A release candidate needs real use before 1.0: run `1.0.0-rc.1` on michi and a couple of real repos for several days. That \"use and iterate\" step isn't compressible.\n4. **External waits.** The next michi release, registry propagation, and npm's holds.\n\nBecause coding is cheap, I'd keep the bar for the v1 promise the same, not widen it to everything cheap. The risk of moving fast is promising more surface, not doing less. The gate list stays the eight items. The soon-after list can slip in alongside if it stays small.\n\n**Next:** I'll start PR 1 (changeset hard error and skipping non-publishable members) and a separate legacy-removal PR for the four items above. Say yes or no on `nuget`, and I'll include it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1819,"cache_read_input_tokens":594583,"output_tokens":1019,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1819,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":594583,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1819},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"887922f2-ab73-42da-a448-3ebf0124dc6f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMUP6gVaWSfSDEddBrNJ","requestRef":"bdb24