026-10-24T17:43:34.424Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/publishing.md:104:- `release` refuses snapshot versions (E169), so a snapshot is never published. Python snapshots use a PEP 440 local label (`0.0.0.dev0+<tag>.<sha>`), which public PyPI would reject anyway. See [PE\ndocs/how-callisto-works.md:23:callisto version --dry-run\ndocs/how-callisto-works.md:35:After reviewing the plan, `callisto version` updates affected manifests, lockfiles, and changelogs. It stages the versioned state for a commit. `callisto release --dry-run` then previews the\ndocs/how-callisto-works.md:51:- **Local release:** `callisto release --dry-run` previews the plan. `callisto release` runs it from a clean checkout.\ndocs/releasing.md:13:- `callisto release --dry-run` prints the plan and performs no effect. It works anywhere, including on a dirty worktree or without an `origin` remote (tags are then noted as unbound).\ndocs/releasing.md:80:- `callisto release --dry-run --format text` — simulates the release plan without effect.\n---\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs:42:/// Builds the exact `cargo publish` argv for one crate: `--manifest-path`\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs:490:/// Classifies combined `cargo publish` output into a [`PublishOutcome`] or\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs:508:        \"cargo publish failed (exit {:?}): {}\",\n156:    // Config membership: a selected member's own reason is often `Changeset` or `UnreleasedVersion`.\n184:/// [`ReleaseInclusionReason::UnreleasedVersion`].\n221:                reasons: vec![ReleaseInclusionReason::UnreleasedVersion],\n313:                reasons: vec![ReleaseInclusionReason::UnreleasedVersion],","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5e3217f7-a541-48fa-874f-445d658f1f15","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users