{"parentUuid":"6115db0a-4d6b-46a7-8866-b0369030b7d3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUbFGWd1E3i2b8YDR4i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2134,"cache_read_input_tokens":597528,"output_tokens":2864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1704},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2134,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2864,"cache_read_input_tokens":597528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2134},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":19786,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"8aace910-784d-4de9-a827-0bfa8da8022a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMUbEsBoTo2RUeScCj1x","requestRef":"8cf39534-eafe-4dfa-bf89-19724086bed4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc28c062-ee5d-4dac-9d6d-f45f42d75422","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:43:55.427Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"dc28c062-ee5d-4dac-9d6d-f45f42d75422","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUbFGWd1E3i2b8YDR4i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, and first publishes deserve their own plan. The core mechanism already exists. A package that has never been released is planned from its manifest version (the `UnreleasedVersion` reason) with no changeset needed. The wiring around it has gaps, and `docs/publishing.md` has no first-publish guidance.\n\n**What makes a first release harder**\n- **Nothing exists yet to compare with.** There's no previous tag, no registry history and no changelog section. Callisto does handle this: the notes fall back to generated, and an absent package is just an absent version. I haven't driven a fresh multi-package repo through it end to end, though.\n- **Bad metadata fails mid-release.** A crate missing `description` or `license` is rejected by `cargo publish`, after earlier crates in the same run may already be live. That is recoverable, because a rerun adopts what landed and finishes the rest, but it is a poor first experience. Today `release --dry-run` doesn't catch it.\n- **Name problems appear only at publish time.** The name may be taken by someone else, or scoped differently than expected. Callisto warns about a foreign repository only when it adopts an already-published version, not when a first publish collides with an existing package of the same name.\n- **Credentials work differently for a new package.** From the registries' docs as I understand them, so please verify before we write them down:\n  - crates.io: trusted publishing needs the crate to exist, so the first publish uses a token.\n  - npm: trusted publishing is configured per existing package, and a granular token must cover the new package's name or scope.\n  - PyPI: a \"pending publisher\" can create the project via OIDC, otherwise an account-wide token is needed once.\n- **Multi-package first releases need ordering and index waits.** The ordering is handled by dependency edges, and `cargo publish` waits for the index itself.\n\n**Proposed scope (small, in the spirit of ship and iterate)**\n1. **Static metadata preflight in `release --dry-run`.** Check what we already parse: crates.io needs `description` and `license`/`license-file`, npm needs a valid name, and PyPI runs `twine check` on the built files. I would not run `cargo publish --dry-run`, because it fails for a dependent crate whose dependency isn't published yet.\n2. **Show \"first publish\" in the plan,** per package, using the existing absent-package observation. Where the registry records a repository for an existing package with the same name, warn if it differs from `origin`. Extend the warning we already have for adopted versions, don't build a new check.\n3. **One \"first publish per registry\" section** in `publishing.md`, plus a pointer in `init` output: token scope, trusted-publisher bootstrap, scoped-package access, and what to expect from the plan.\n4. **Make this the rehearsal.** The end-to-end run I proposed should be exactly this: a fresh scratch repo with a never-published Cargo + npm + Python workspace. Local registries (Verdaccio, pypiserver, cargo-http-registry) can prove the mechanics. Your credentials and real names are needed only for the final check.\n\n**What I would not build**\n- Token-scope probing or automating trusted-publisher setup. Both are registry-side and change often.\n- A dry-run that compiles and verifies every crate.\n- A special \"bootstrap mode\" or command. The normal flow should just work.\n\nShould I add this as a fifth PR in the sequence, after the changeset and allow-list fixes? I'd write the fresh-repo rehearsal first, since it shows which of these gaps are real before we fix any."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2134,"cache_read_input_tokens":597528,"output_tokens":2864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1704},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2134,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2864,"cache_read_input_tokens":597528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2134},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8aace910-784d-4de9-a827-0bfa8da8022a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMUbEsBoTo2RUeScCj1x","requestRef":"8cf39534-eafe-4dfa-bf89-19724086bed4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"229911e9-e268-4b4a-906c-ea54fa6f4d1d","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:43:59.654Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
