{"parentUuid":"5e0a88e9-b90b-4c86-b659-5f2e0d3a8770","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9060f1dc-711c-48e3-8f57-8ca746997cbc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XZhqA8ied6tZKQfPQMxcks","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PyPI file name reuse deleted release cannot re-upload same filename; yank PEP 592; delete project name\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Help · TestPyPI\",\"url\":\"https://test.pypi.org/help/\"},{\"title\":\"PEP 694\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/\"},{\"title\":\"PEP 541\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0541/\"},{\"title\":\"reuse · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/reuse/\"},{\"title\":\"fsfe-reuse · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/fsfe-reuse/\"},{\"title\":\"Project Quarantine - The Python Package Index Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.pypi.org/posts/2024-12-30-quarantine/\"},{\"title\":\"PEP 763\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0763/\"},{\"title\":\"guessfilename · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/guessfilename/\"},{\"title\":\"rename · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/rename/\"},{\"title\":\"copyparty · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/copyparty/1.6.10/\"}]\n\nThe search turned up consistent answers on the filename rule, though nothing directly about PEP 592's yank spec itself.\n\n**Filenames can't be reused, even after deletion.** PyPI's help page says that PyPI does not allow for a filename to be reused, even once a project has been deleted and recreated. That page is on TestPyPI, but it describes the rule that applies to PyPI's filename namespace. It also says that deleted files cannot be re-uploaded. The recommended fix is to bump the version number, rebuild, and upload again, since a distribution filename is the combination of project name, version number, and distribution type.\n\n**Deleting a project releases its name.** The same help page says that deletion of a project makes it uninstallable, and releases the project name for use by any other PyPI user. Deletions are permanent: deleted projects, releases or files cannot be restored by PyPI administrators. Despite that, the filename stays blocked.\n\n**Yank (PEP 592) as the alternative.** PEP 763 proposes that a project, release, or file may only be deleted within 72 hours of when it is uploaded to the index. After that window, users may only use the \"yank\" mechanism specified by PEP 592. PEP 763 is a proposal, so check whether it has been accepted before relying on the 72-hour rule. The yank mechanism itself is only referenced here, not described.\n\n**Atomicity and conflicts (PEP 694).** The Upload 2.0 API draft says that the index MUST guarantee that it never publishes two files with the same name for the same release, and rejects duplicates with a 409 Conflict.\n\n**Name retention (PEP 541)** is a separate matter. Reclaiming a project name from an abandoned project is governed by criteria that are more stringent for a different project than for continued maintenance of the same one.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bff44ee0-99ba-40f4-9c26-b69a828a6621","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:45:08.288Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"PyPI file name reuse deleted release cannot re-upload same filename; yank PEP 592; delete project name","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LDQiXtb1zpsYmm8FrinydF","content":[{"title":"Help · TestPyPI","url":"https://test.pypi.org/help/"},{"title":"PEP 694","url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0694/"},{"title":"PEP 541","url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0541/"},{"title":"reuse · PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/reuse/"},{"title":"fsfe-reuse · PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/fsfe-reuse/"},{"title":"Project Quarantine - The Python Package Index Blog","url":"https://blog.pypi.org/posts/2024-12-30-quarantine/"},{"title":"PEP 763","url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0763/"},{"title":"guessfilename · PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/guessfilename/"},{"title":"rename · PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/rename/"},{"title":"copyparty · PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/copyparty/1.6.10/"}]},"The search turned up consistent answers on the filename rule, though nothing directly about PEP 592's yank spec itself.\n\n**Filenames can't be reused, even after deletion.** PyPI's help page says that PyPI does not allow for a filename to be reused, even once a project has been deleted and recreated. That page is on TestPyPI, but it describes the rule that applies to PyPI's filename namespace. It also says that deleted files cannot be re-uploaded. The recommended fix is to bump the version number, rebuild, and upload again, since a distribution filename is the combination of project name, version number, and distribution type.\n\n**Deleting a project releases its name.** The same help page says that deletion of a project makes it uninstallable, and releases the project name for use by any other PyPI user. Deletions are permanent: deleted projects, releases or files cannot be restored by PyPI administrators. Despite that, the filename stays blocked.\n\n**Yank (PEP 592) as the alternative.** PEP 763 proposes that a project, release, or file may only be deleted within 72 hours of when it is uploaded to the index. After that window, users may only use the \"yank\" mechanism specified by PEP 592. PEP 763 is a proposal, so check whether it has been accepted before relying on the 72-hour rule. The yank mechanism itself is only referenced here, not described.\n\n**Atomicity and conflicts (PEP 694).** The Upload 2.0 API draft says that the index MUST guarantee that it never publishes two files with the same name for the same release, and rejects duplicates with a 409 Conflict.\n\n**Name retention (PEP 541)** is a separate matter. Reclaiming a project name from an abandoned project is governed by criteria that are more stringent for a different project than for continued maintenance of the same one."],"durationSeconds":6.665181457996368,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"beec4516-98a6-4dc1-a25d-ca66a3567dbc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e0a88e9-b90b-4c86-b659-5f2e0d3a8770","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
