{"parentUuid":"1d4bb0a2-3e6f-407d-8627-49e7ef12a17a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUiAYS8CoFCJMPWjm8y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DzfMXEia5dEsNja24pwonX","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"crates.io policy owner can delete crate: less than 500 downloads per version or published less than 72 hours ago, no reverse dependencies","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1681,"cache_read_input_tokens":605925,"output_tokens":173,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":57},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1681,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":173,"cache_read_input_tokens":605925,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1681},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DzfMXEia5dEsNja24pwonX":{"query":"crates.io policy owner can delete crate: less than 500 downloads per version or published less than 72 hours ago, no reverse dependencies","mode":"standard"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1a9b635c-6852-4be6-abfb-c4df01d9c2f6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMUiA5ALsqnrVXWqUYBN","requestRef":"f028f236-b09a-429c-93f6-8aac31f3ce2e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15567716-226d-453b-b706-39727bc8545a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:45:11.284Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"15567716-226d-453b-b706-39727bc8545a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9060f1dc-711c-48e3-8f57-8ca746997cbc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DzfMXEia5dEsNja24pwonX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"crates.io policy owner can delete crate: less than 500 downloads per version or published less than 72 hours ago, no reverse dependencies\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"www.crates.io\",\"url\":\"https://www.crates.io/policies\"},{\"title\":\"crates.io: development update\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/02/05/crates-io-development-update/\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rust-lang/blog.rust-lang.org/pull/1471.diff\"},{\"title\":\"Keyboard shortcuts\",\"url\":\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3660-crates-io-crate-deletions.html\"},{\"title\":\"Future of the gtk-rs repositories for GTK3 and VTE3: Will gtk3, gtk-sys, and vte-sys be removed?\",\"url\":\"https://users.rust-lang.org/t/future-of-the-gtk-rs-repositories-for-gtk3-and-vte3-will-gtk3-gtk-sys-and-vte-sys-be-removed/142065\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io/pull/9904\"},{\"title\":\"3660 crates io crate deletions\",\"url\":\"https://www.rustmax.net/library/rfcs/3660-crates-io-crate-deletions\"},{\"title\":\"[Pre-RFC] Crates expropriation policy\",\"url\":\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-crates-expropriation-policy/8668\"},{\"title\":\"[RFC3660] Crate Deletions New small proposal\",\"url\":\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/rfc3660-crate-deletions-new-small-proposal/22427\"}]\n\nThe live crates.io policy and the Rust blog both support the thresholds you describe, with two corrections: the download limit is per month, not per version, and the single-owner condition is part of the rule.\n\n- **Time window:** A crate published within the last 72 hours can be deleted by its owners. The policy page lists the 72-hour window alongside a single-owner, download, and no-dependents set of conditions.\n- **Download threshold:** The current policy sets the limit at 500 downloads, measured for each month it has been published, so a crate's total is compared against 500 times its months since publication. The 2025 Rust blog post describes the same rule and says the requirements were put in place to prevent abuse of the deletion feature.\n- **Single owner:** Your summary omits this condition. The policy page and the blog both include it, and the blog's wording suggests it must be met alongside the download and dependency checks. The policy page's wording is looser, which makes the logic ambiguous.\n- **Reverse dependencies:** The crate must not be depended upon by any other crate on crates.io.\n- **Discrepancies in older sources:** The original RFC 3660 proposal set the limit at 100 downloads per month, and a forum post quoted a 1000-download figure. The current policy text in these results says 500, so the older numbers appear superseded. A crates.io pull request also refers to 100 downloads per month, which likely reflects the RFC rather than the final rule.\n- **Exceptions:** Outside these conditions, owners may contact the crates.io team to request deletion of a crate.\n\nSo the accurate rule is: deletable if published under 72 hours ago, or if the crate has a single owner, fewer than 500 downloads per published month, and no reverse dependencies. I could not check the live policy page directly, so confirm the current wording there before relying on it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c508faaa-3f5b-4729-8c7a-9b80614e96e5","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:45:20.258Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"crates.io policy owner can delete crate: less than 500 downloads per version or published less than 72 hours ago, no reverse dependencies","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EMj1jaFcNmbD4EbDhL8Vec","content":[{"title":"www.crates.io","url":"https://www.crates.io/policies"},{"title":"crates.io: development update","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/02/05/crates-io-development-update/"},{"title":"github.com","url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/blog.rust-lang.org/pull/1471.diff"},{"title":"Keyboard shortcuts","url":"https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3660-crates-io-crate-deletions.html"},{"title":"Future of the gtk-rs repositories for GTK3 and VTE3: Will gtk3, gtk-sys, and vte-sys be removed?","url":"https://users.rust-lang.org/t/future-of-the-gtk-rs-repositories-for-gtk3-and-vte3-will-gtk3-gtk-sys-and-vte-sys-be-removed/142065"},{"title":"github.com","url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io/pull/9904"},{"title":"3660 crates io crate deletions","url":"https://www.rustmax.net/library/rfcs/3660-crates-io-crate-deletions"},{"title":"[Pre-RFC] Crates expropriation policy","url":"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-crates-expropriation-policy/8668"},{"title":"[RFC3660] Crate Deletions New small proposal","url":"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/rfc3660-crate-deletions-new-small-proposal/22427"}]},"The live crates.io policy and the Rust blog both support the thresholds you describe, with two corrections: the download limit is per month, not per version, and the single-owner condition is part of the rule.\n\n- **Time window:** A crate published within the last 72 hours can be deleted by its owners. The policy page lists the 72-hour window alongside a single-owner, download, and no-dependents set of conditions.\n- **Download threshold:** The current policy sets the limit at 500 downloads, measured for each month it has been published, so a crate's total is compared against 500 times its months since publication. The 2025 Rust blog post describes the same rule and says the requirements were put in place to prevent abuse of the deletion feature.\n- **Single owner:** Your summary omits this condition. The policy page and the blog both include it, and the blog's wording suggests it must be met alongside the download and dependency checks. The policy page's wording is looser, which makes the logic ambiguous.\n- **Reverse dependencies:** The crate must not be depended upon by any other crate on crates.io.\n- **Discrepancies in older sources:** The original RFC 3660 proposal set the limit at 100 downloads per month, and a forum post quoted a 1000-download figure. The current policy text in these results says 500, so the older numbers appear superseded. A crates.io pull request also refers to 100 downloads per month, which likely reflects the RFC rather than the final rule.\n- **Exceptions:** Outside these conditions, owners may contact the crates.io team to request deletion of a crate.\n\nSo the accurate rule is: deletable if published under 72 hours ago, or if the crate has a single owner, fewer than 500 downloads per published month, and no reverse dependencies. I could not check the live policy page directly, so confirm the current wording there before relying on it."],"durationSeconds":8.23240429198742,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1a9b635c-6852-4be6-abfb-c4df01d9c2f6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15567716-226d-453b-b706-39727bc8545a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"cl