{"parentUuid":"a8bf6a3d-f95e-42fc-a9a1-2ba4b93e73ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"32b2f8eb-0442-4844-9280-8f2845420a76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AHrzttQoETxooRDMJC3mQ1","type":"tool_result","content":"##### init --help\nScaffold Callisto configuration in the current workspace\n\nUsage: callisto init [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --format <FORMAT>                Output format for command results [default: text] [possible values: text, json]\n      --yes                            Run without prompts; required when stdin is not a terminal\n      --cwd <CWD>                      Workspace directory to operate in (defaults to the current directory) [default: .]\n      --versioning <VERSIONING>        Whether packages share one version (fixed) or version independently [possible values: fixed, independent]\n      --artifact-target <TRIPLE>       Ship the product's binaries as GitHub release assets for this Rust target triple (repeatable, comma-separated)\n      --dry-run                        Preview manifest and file changes without writing to disk\n      --product-package <PACKAGE>      The package whose binaries ship, when several packages produce one\n      --forge-repository <OWNER/REPO>  The GitHub repository (`owner/repo`) binaries are released to\n      --workflow                       Generate `.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml`\n      --no-workflow                    Do not generate a GitHub Actions release workflow\n  -h, --help                           Print help\n\n##### A: single crate, plain 'init' (non-interactive stdin)\nDetected:\n  ecosystems: cargo\n  origin: https://github.com/example/single.git\n  packages:\n    cargo/single 0.1.0 (last tag: none)\nE240\n\n  × stdin is not a terminal, so init needs flags instead of prompts; missing:\n  │ --yes, --versioning\n  help: re-run `callisto init --yes` with the listed flags, or run it in a\n        terminal to be asked\n\n--- A: init --yes (no flags)\