{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","id":"b9a3f609-94a8-45f2-be7b-12a6686571a5","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:46:37.016Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"761156c7f8e5f9beaaf03c55d45c00e6108ed5cc90a785040747ceaf99aae387","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"93acba71-cfa9-4918-9987-67b5ad8e1d12","keep":950,"tail":["cbfb9e4db54a3efcf34d9208d91a71a7c813f8e500302cecf205a28d40d8aef2","6add62ca95fc46c3519107979928a9db503f1687871ebe1e36fd618272092b67","5aaa5080eea835650b489283e179d812aa36392550a40c66275476fb444fcfcd"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",952,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"144c7fc0eca3c06ed0c21c93cbf44b73f004e6ffd230cd59bcab2b8e6c14106c"}
{"parentUuid":"e5718490-810e-4837-98a9-f5244435603a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUphgboVEetznWDNRP6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran `init` on three scratch repos (a single crate, an npm + Python monorepo, and a mixed workspace) and found three problems. The mechanics are good, and I'd harden around them without adding much.\n\n## What works well\n- **`callisto.toml` is just a comment.** The defaults carry everything, and `status` and `release --dry-run` work straight away. The mixed repo planned npm and PyPI publishes with no configuration, and the private workspace root was correctly left out.\n- **The generated workflow is small** (about 30 lines) and pinned to a commit SHA, with secrets only on the release step.\n- **`init` prints the detected packages and a one-line reminder** to require reviews on `main`.\n\n## What I found\n1. **A name collision on a first release gives a misleading error.**\n   - My scratch crate was called `single`. crates.io already has a crate by that name, version 0.1.0, from someone else (`CAD97/rust-single`).\n   - `release --dry-run` said: \"`cargo/single` 0.1.0 is already published… Check out 3e7c70b… and run `callisto release` again to finish that release.\"\n   - That is exactly the wrong advice for a new user. It sends them to finish a release they never made, when the name belongs to someone else's project.\n   - Callisto does have a foreign-repository check, but it only fires when it adopts a version, and here the E320 path ran first.\n2. **`init` demands `--versioning` even for a single package,** where fixed versus independent means nothing. Both `init` on a non-terminal and `init --yes` fail with E240 or E241 until it is supplied.\n3. **No \"what do I do next\" after `init`.** The output doesn't clearly list the secrets to add per detected registry, link a first-publish guide, or suggest the first commands. There is also no single check that says \"you are ready to release\" versus \"this name is taken.\"\n\n## Recommended changes (defaults first, expert settings stay opt-in)\n\n**Defaults**\n- **Versioning:** don't ask for a single package, and default to `independent` for several packages. Keep `--versioning` as the expert override.\n- **Workflow:** generate it by default when `origin` is a GitHub URL. `--no-workflow` still opts out.\n- **Non-interactive:** `init --yes` with no other flags should just work in the common case.\n- **Next steps:** print the exact secret names for the registries detected (for example `NPM_TOKEN`, `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`), the first commands (`callisto add`, `callisto release --dry-run`), and a pointer to the first-publish section.\n\n**First-release safety, folded into `release --dry-run` (no new command)**\n- When a package name exists on the registry under a different repository than `origin`, say so before anything else: \"the name `single` is taken by another project; rename the package.\" This replaces the misleading E320 for that case.\n- The metadata checks I proposed earlier (description, license, valid name, `twine check`).\n\n**Expert configuration**\n- Keep `callisto.toml` additive and optional. In `docs/config.md`, mark every key as \"default / when you need it\", so beginners can ignore the page.\n- Add one short \"advanced\" section for the things people actually need: registry URLs and timeouts, tag templates for renames, fixed or linked groups, and artifact targets.\n\n**Tests that lock this in**\n- A scripted \"first ten minutes\" matrix: single crate, npm monorepo, Python-only, mixed, an existing `@changesets/cli` repo being migrated, and a repo with a taken name. Each case runs `init`, then `add`, then `release --dry-run`, and asserts the output. This is also the end-to-end rehearsal we already planned.\n\n## What I'd skip (over-engineering)\n- A `doctor` command, an interactive TUI redesign, or a generated config schema. The next-steps output and the dry-run checks cover the same ground.\n- Token-scope probing or automating trusted-publisher setup.\n- Probing for secrets in GitHub from the CLI. It needs extra permissions and breaks the \"no credentials in the tool\" model.\n\n## Decisions for you\n1. Should `init` write the workflow by default for GitHub remotes, or keep asking? I'd default to writing it.\n2. Is `independent` the right default for several packages? It matches changesets. The alternative is asking only when more than one package is found.\n\nI'd start with the `init` defaults, the next-steps output and the taken-name diagnosis, since all three are small and visible in the first minute of use. Should I fold this into the first-release PR set?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1843,"cache_read_input_tokens":618628,"output_tokens":1495,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1495,"cache_read_input_tokens":618628,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"eb075ed6-bfbc-4a5b-9a61-9556f1651991","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMUphJY2EDFCXseont6f","requestRef":"b9a3f609-94a8-45f2-be7b-12a6686571a5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3af61b1-6a31-4633-b0e9-357b67dbe428","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:46:49.644Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
