{"parentUuid":"83cd3dd7-83a9-494c-bffa-d11f6fc4d59a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"292a1ddc-3040-4aad-8fec-ec43ab952564","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q6JoCmUU6eYwSdDLbpeBDz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! `callisto init`: report detected facts, ask only for intent, preview the first release, then write.\n2\t\n3\tuse std::io::Write;\n4\tuse std::process::ExitCode;\n5\t\n6\tuse callisto_graph::commands::init::{\n7\t    self as scaffold, BinaryRelease, InitAnswers, InitFacts, InitPackage, Versioning,\n8\t};\n9\tuse callisto_graph::locate::IgnoreWalkLocator;\n10\tuse callisto_graph::GraphError;\n11\tuse callisto_model::{ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, InitReport, SCHEMA_VERSION};\n12\tuse dialoguer::{Confirm, Input, Select};\n13\t\n14\tuse crate::cli::{GlobalArgs, InitArgs, InitVersioning, OutputFormat};\n15\tuse crate::error::CliError;\n16\tuse crate::output::emit_report;\n17\tuse crate::render;\n18\tuse crate::runner::CliCommandRunner;\n19\tuse crate::tty;\n20\tuse crate::workspace::workspace_root;\n21\t\n22\tpub const VERSIONING_PROMPT: &str = \"How should packages be versioned?\";\n23\tpub const SHIP_PROMPT: &str = \"Ship binaries as GitHub release assets?\";\n24\tpub const PRODUCT_PROMPT: &str = \"Which package is the product whose binaries ship?\";\n25\tpub const FORGE_PROMPT: &str = \"GitHub repository to release to (owner/repo)\";\n26\tpub const TARGETS_PROMPT: &str = \"Artifact target triples (comma-separated)\";\n27\tpub const WRITE_PROMPT: &str = \"Write callisto.toml?\";\n28\tpub const WORKFLOW_PROMPT: &str = \"Generate a GitHub Actions release workflow?\";\n29\t/// Printed instead of the preview when the repository has no commit to plan from.\n30\tpub const NO_COMMITS: &str =\n31\t    \"No commits yet: commit, then run `callisto release --dry-run` to preview the first release.\";\n32\t/// Printed instead of asking `WORKFLOW_PROMPT` for a workspace no generated workflow covers.\n33\tfn workflow_unsupported_note(reason: scaffold::WorkflowUnsupported) -> String {\n34\t    format!(\"Skipping GitHub Actions workflow generation: {reason}.\")\n35\t}\n36\t/// Printed once a generated workflow is written: a merge to `branch` is the release approval.\n37\tfn merge_publishes_note(branch: &str) -> String {\n38\t    format!(\n39\t        \"Merging to `{branch}` publishes: require pull requests and reviews on `{branch}` (GitHub → Settings → Rules).\"\n40\t    )\n41\t}\n42\tconst VERSIONING_CHOICES: [&str; 2] = [\n43\t    \"independent: each package has its own version\",\n44\t    \"fixed: every package shares one version\",\n45\t];\n46\t\n47\t/// Asks the operator questions; a scripted implementation drives tests.\n48\tpub trait Prompter {\n49\t    fn select(&mut self, prompt: &str, items: &[String]) -> Result<usize, CliError>;\n50\t    fn confirm(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: bool) -> Result<bool, CliError>;\n51\t    fn input(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: Option<&str>) -> Result<String, CliError>;\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\tstruct TerminalPrompter;\n55\t\n56\timpl Prompter for TerminalPrompter {\n57\t    fn select(&mut self, prompt: &str, items: &[String]) -> Result<usize, CliError> {\n58\t        Ok(Select::new().with_prompt(prompt).items(items).default(0).interact()?)\n59\t    }\n60\t\n61\t    fn confirm(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: bool) -> Result<bool, CliError> {\n62\t        Ok(Confirm::new().with_prompt(prompt).default(default).interact()?)\n63\t    }\n64\t\n65\t    fn input(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: Option<&str>) -> Result<String, CliError> {\n66\t        let mut input = Input::<String>::new().with_prompt(prompt);\n67\t        if let Some(default) = default {\n68\t            input = input.default(default.to_owned());\n69\t        }\n70\t        Ok(input.interact_text()?)\n71\t    }\n72\t}\n73\t\n74\tpub fn handle(args: InitArgs, global: &GlobalArgs) -> Result<ExitCode, CliError> {\n75\t    run(\n76\t        args,\n77\t        global,\n78\t        tty::is_interactive(),\n79\t        &mut TerminalPrompter,\n80\t        &mut std::io::stdout(),\n81\t        &mut std::io::stderr(),\n82\t        &CliCommandRunner,\n83\t    )\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t/// `init` against explicit terminal state, prompter, output streams, and command runner.\n87\tpub fn run<R: CommandRunner>(\n88\t    args: InitArgs,\n89\t    global: &GlobalArgs,\n90\t    interactive: bool,\n91\t    prompter: &mut dyn Prompter,\n92\t    out: &mut dyn Write,\n93\t    err: &mut dyn Write,\n94\t    runner: &R,\n95\t) -> Result<ExitCode, CliError> {\n96\t    validate_flags(&args)?;\n97\t    let root = workspace_root(global, runner)?;\n98\t    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(&root);\n99\t    let facts = scaffold::detect(&root, &locator, runner)?;\n100\t    let json = global.format == OutputFormat::Json;\n101\t    // JSON keeps stdout for the report.\n102\t    let human: &mut dyn Write = if json { &mut *err } else { &mut *out };\n103\t    write_facts(&facts, human)?;\n104\t\n105\t    if facts.origin.is_none() {\n106\t        if args.workflow {\n107\t            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresOrigin { flag: \"workflow\" });\n108\t        }\n109\t        if !args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n110\t            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresOrigin {\n111\t                flag: \"artifact-target\",\n112\t            });\n113\t        }\n114\t    }\n115\t    if !interactive && !args.yes {\n116\t        let mut missing = vec![\"--yes\"];\n117\t        missing.extend(missing_flags(&args, &facts));\n118\t        return Err(CliError::InitRequiresYes { missing });\n119\t    }\n120\t    if args.yes {\n121\t        let missing = missing_flags(&args, &facts);\n122\t        if !missing.is_empty() {\n123\t            return Err(CliError::InitMissingFlags { missing });\n124\t        }\n125\t    }\n126\t    let prompting = interactive && !args.yes;\n127\t    let answers = collect_answers(&args, &facts, prompting, prompter)?;\n128\t\n129\t    let mut diagnostics = scaffold::changesets_config_diagnostics(&facts.root);\n130\t    if facts.origin.is_none() {\n131\t        writeln!(human, \"{ORIGIN_MISSING_NOTE}\")?;\n132\t        diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n133\t            code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::InitOriginMissing,\n134\t            severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n135\t            message: ORIGIN_MISSING_NOTE.to_owned(),\n136\t            package: None,\n137\t            path: None,\n138\t            escalated_by: None,\n139\t            governed_by: None,\n140\t        });\n141\t    }\n142\t    let shape = match scaffold::workflow_shape(&facts, &answers) {\n143\t        Err(reason) if args.workflow => {\n144\t            return Err(GraphError::InitWorkflowUnsupported {\n145\t                reason: reason.to_string(),\n146\t            }\n147\t            .into());\n148\t        }\n149\t        Err(reason) => {\n150\t            let note = workflow_unsupported_note(reason);\n151\t            writeln!(human, \"{note}\")?;\n152\t            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n153\t                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::WorkflowGenerationUnsupported,\n154\t                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n155\t                message: note,\n156\t                package: None,\n157\t                path: None,\n158\t                escalated_by: None,\n159\t                governed_by: None,\n160\t            });\n161\t            None\n162\t        }\n163\t        Ok(shape) => Some(shape),\n164\t    };\n165\t    let want_workflow = match shape {\n166\t        None => false,\n167\t        Some(_) if args.workflow => true,\n168\t        Some(_) if args.no_workflow => false,\n169\t        Some(_) if prompting && facts.origin.is_some() => prompter.confirm(WORKFLOW_PROMPT, false)?,\n170\t        Some(_) => false,\n171\t    };\n172\t    let workflow = match shape.filter(|_| want_workflow) {\n173\t        Some(shape) => {\n174\t            scaffold::ensure_workflow_absent(&facts.root)?;\n175\t            let branch = scaffold::default_branch(runner, &facts.root);\n176\t            writeln!(human, \"  default branch: {} (from {})\", branch.name, branch.source)?;\n177\t            let version = env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\");\n178\t            let commit = scaffold::resolve_release_commit(runner, &facts.root, version)?;\n179\t            let content = scaffold::render_workflow(&facts, shape, &branch.name, &commit, version);\n180\t            Some((content, branch.name))\n181\t        }\n182\t        None => None,\n183\t    };\n184\t\n185\t    let config = scaffold::render_config(&facts, &answers);\n186\t    let plan = if facts.has_commit {\n187\t        Some(scaffold::preview(&facts, &config, &locator, runner)?)\n188\t    } else {\n189\t        None\n190\t    };\n191\t    writeln!(human, \"\\ncallisto.toml:\\n{config}\")?;\n192\t    match plan {\n193\t        Some(plan) => {\n194\t            writeln!(human, \"First release preview (`callisto release --dry-run`):\")?;\n195\t            super::release::write_release_preview(plan.as_ref(), OutputFormat::Text, human)?;\n196\t        }\n197\t        None => writeln!(human, \"{NO_COMMITS}\")?,\n198\t    }\n199\t    if let Some((workflow, _)) = &workflow {\n200\t        writeln!(\n201\t            human,\n202\t            \"\\n{}:\\n{workflow}\",\n203\t            scaffold::workflow_path(&facts.root).display()\n204\t        )?;\n205\t    }\n206\t\n207\t    // Computed before any write, so the `.changeset/README.md` existence check sees disk state as-is.\n208\t    let files = scaffold::init_files(&facts.root, workflow.is_some())?;\n209\t    let mut report = if global.dry_run {\n210\t        InitReport {\n211\t            schema_version: SCHEMA_VERSION,\n212\t            initialized: false,\n213\t            config_path: facts.root.join(\"callisto.toml\"),\n214\t            config,\n215\t            files,\n216\t            diagnostics: Vec::new(),\n217\t        }\n218\t    } else {\n219\t        if prompting && !prompter.confirm(WRITE_PROMPT, true)? {\n220\t            writeln!(human, \"Initialization cancelled; nothing was written.\")?;\n221\t            return Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS);\n222\t        }\n223\t        let permit = ApplyPermit::granted_unless_dry_run(global.dry_run).expect(\"non-dry-run permits writes\");\n224\t        let mut report = scaffold::write(&facts.root, &config, &permit)?;\n225\t        if let Some((workflow, branch)) = &workflow {\n226\t            scaffold::write_workflow(&facts.root, workflow, &permit)?;\n227\t            let note = merge_publishes_note(branch);\n228\t            writeln!(human, \"{note}\")?;\n229\t            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n230\t                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::WorkflowMergePublishes,\n231\t                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Info,\n232\t                message: note,\n233\t                package: None,\n234\t                path: None,\n235\t                escalated_by: None,\n236\t                governed_by: None,\n237\t            });\n238\t        }\n239\t        report.files = files;\n240\t        report\n241\t    };\n242\t    report.diagnostics.extend(diagnostics);\n243\t    if json {\n244\t        emit_report(&mut &mut *out, &report, global.dry_run)?;\n245\t    } else {\n246\t        render::render_init(&report, &mut &mut *out)?;\n247\t    }\n248\t    Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS)\n249\t}\n250\t\n251\t/// Printed, and recorded as a warning diagnostic, when no `origin` remote is configured.\n252\tconst ORIGIN_MISSING_NOTE: &str = \"No `origin` remote is configured: skipping the release workflow and \\\n253\tshipping-binaries questions; `callisto release` will refuse until one is added.\";\n254\t\n255\t/// Rejects flag combinations invalid regardless of workspace facts.\n256\tfn validate_flags(args: &InitArgs) -> Result<(), CliError> {\n257\t    if args.workflow && args.no_workflow {\n258\t        return Err(CliError::InitWorkflowFlagsConflict);\n259\t    }\n260\t    if args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n261\t        if args.forge_repository.is_some() {\n262\t            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresArtifactTarget {\n263\t                flag: \"forge-repository\",\n264\t            });\n265\t        }\n266\t        if args.product_package.is_some() {\n267\t            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresArtifactTarget {\n268\t                flag: \"product-package\",\n269\t            });\n270\t        }\n271\t    }\n272\t    Ok(())\n273\t}\n274\t\n275\tfn write_facts(facts: &InitFacts, out: &mut dyn Write) -> Result<(), CliError> {\n276\t    let ecosystems: Vec<&str> = facts.ecosystems.iter().map(|ecosystem| ecosystem.prefix()).collect();\n277\t    writeln!(out, \"Detected:\")?;\n278\t    writeln!(out, \"  ecosystems: {}\", ecosystems.join(\", \"))?;\n279\t    writeln!(out, \"  origin: {}\", facts.origin.as_deref().unwrap_or(\"none\"))?;\n280\t    writeln!(out, \"  packages:\")?;\n281\t    for package in &facts.packages {\n282\t        let tag = package.last_tag.as_ref().map_or(\"none\", |tag| tag.as_str());\n283\t        write!(out, \"    {} {} (last tag: {tag}\", package.id, package.version)?;\n284\t        if package.is_binary() {\n285\t            write!(out, \"; binary: {}\", package.bin_names.join(\", \"))?;\n286\t        }\n287\t        writeln!(out, \")\")?;\n288\t    }\n289\t    Ok(())\n290\t}\n291\t\n292\t/// Flags `--yes` needs that were not supplied.\n293\tfn missing_flags(args: &InitArgs, facts: &InitFacts) -> Vec<&'static str> {\n294\t    let mut missing = Vec::new();\n295\t    if args.versioning.is_none() {\n296\t        missing.push(\"--versioning\");\n297\t    }\n298\t    if !args.artifact_targets.is_empty() && facts.binary_packages().next().is_some() {\n299\t        if args.forge_repository.is_none() {\n300\t            missing.push(\"--forge-repository\");\n301\t        }\n302\t        if args.product_package.is_none() && facts.binary_packages().nth(1).is_some() {\n303\t            missing.push(\"--product-package\");\n304\t        }\n305\t    }\n306\t    missing\n307\t}\n308\t\n309\tfn missing(flag: &'static str) -> CliError {\n310\t    CliError::InitMissingFlags { missing: vec![flag] }\n311\t}\n312\t\n313\tfn collect_answers(\n314\t    args: &InitArgs,\n315\t    facts: &InitFacts,\n316\t    prompting: bool,\n317\t    prompter: &mut dyn Prompter,\n318\t) -> Result<InitAnswers, CliError> {\n319\t    let versioning = match args.versioning {\n320\t        Some(InitVersioning::Fixed) => Versioning::Fixed,\n321\t        Some(InitVersioning::Independent) => Versioning::Independent,\n322\t        None if prompting => {\n323\t            let choices: Vec<String> = VERSIONING_CHOICES.iter().map(|choice| (*choice).to_owned()).collect();\n324\t            match prompter.select(VERSIONING_PROMPT, &choices)? {\n325\t                0 => Versioning::Independent,\n326\t                _ => Versioning::Fixed,\n327\t            }\n328\t        }\n329\t        None => return Err(missing(\"--versioning\")),\n330\t    };\n331\t    let no_binaries = InitAnswers {\n332\t        versioning,\n333\t        binaries: None,\n334\t    };\n335\t\n336\t    let binaries: Vec<&InitPackage> = facts.binary_packages().collect();\n337\t    if binaries.is_empty() && !args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n338\t        if let Some(package) = facts.unsupported_artifact_packages().next() {\n339\t            return Err(GraphError::InitUnsupportedArtifactBuilder {\n340\t                package: package.id.clone(),\n341\t                ecosystem: package\n342\t                    .id\n343\t                    .split_once('/')\n344\t                    .map_or(\"unknown\", |(ecosystem, _)| ecosystem)\n345\t                    .to_owned(),\n346\t            }\n347\t            .into());\n348\t        }\n349\t        return Err(GraphError::InitNoBinaryPackage.into());\n350\t    }\n351\t    let requested_product = args\n352\t        .product_package\n353\t        .as_deref()\n354\t        .map(|name| facts.product_package(name))\n355\t        .transpose()?;\n356\t    if binaries.is_empty() {\n357\t        return Ok(no_binaries);\n358\t    }\n359\t    // No `origin`: the forge question below has nothing to validate a repository against, so\n360\t    // shipping is never offered (skips straight to `no_binaries`); `--artifact-target` without\n361\t    // `origin` is already rejected up front in `run`.\n362\t    let ship = !args.artifact_targets.is_empty()\n363\t        || (facts.origin.is_some() && prompting && prompter.confirm(SHIP_PROMPT, false)?);\n364\t    if !ship {\n365\t        return Ok(no_binaries);\n366\t    }\n367\t\n368\t    let product = match (requested_product, binaries.as_slice()) {\n369\t        (Some(product), _) => product,\n370\t        (None, [only]) => only,\n371\t        (None, _) if prompting => {\n372\t            let ids: Vec<String> = binaries.iter().map(|package| package.id.clone()).collect();\n373\t            binaries[prompter.select(PRODUCT_PROMPT, &ids)?]\n374\t        }\n375\t        (None, _) => return Err(missing(\"--product-package\")),\n376\t    };\n377\t\n378\t    let forge_repository = match &args.forge_repository {\n379\t        Some(value) => scaffold::forge_repository(facts, value)?,\n380\t        None if prompting => {\n381\t            let detected = facts.origin_repository.as_ref().map(|repository| repository.as_slug());\n382\t            scaffold::forge_repository(facts, &prompter.input(FORGE_PROMPT, detected.as_deref())?)?\n383\t        }\n384\t        None => return Err(missing(\"--forge-repository\")),\n385\t    };\n386\t\n387\t    let targets = if args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n388\t        loop {\n389\t            let answer = prompter.input(TARGETS_PROMPT, None)?;\n390\t            let targets: Vec<String> = answer.split(',').map(str::trim).map(str::to_owned).collect();\n391\t            if targets.iter().all(|target| target.is_empty()) {\n392\t                // Nothing meaningful submitted: re-ask rather than error.\n393\t                continue;\n394\t            }\n395\t            break targets;\n396\t        }\n397\t    } else {\n398\t        args.artifact_targets.clone()\n399\t    };\n400\t    let targets = scaffold::validate_targets(&targets)?;\n401\t\n402\t    Ok(InitAnswers {\n403\t        versioning,\n404\t        binaries: Some(BinaryRelease {\n405\t            product: product.id.clone(),\n406\t            forge_repository,\n407\t            targets,\n408\t        }),\n409\t    })\n410\t}\n411\t\n412\t#[cfg(test)]\n413\tmod tests;\n414\t"}]},"uuid":"6c3f3418-a8b5-45a6-a3ad-90fad18bcbfa","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:50:36.360Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/init.rs","content":"//! `callisto init`: report detected facts, ask only for intent, preview the first release, then write.\n\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::process::ExitCode;\n\nuse callisto_graph::commands::init::{\n    self as scaffold, BinaryRelease, InitAnswers, InitFacts, InitPackage, Versioning,\n};\nuse callisto_graph::locate::IgnoreWalkLocator;\nuse callisto_graph::GraphError;\nuse callisto_model::{ApplyPermit, CommandRunner, InitReport, SCHEMA_VERSION};\nuse dialoguer::{Confirm, Input, Select};\n\nuse crate::cli::{GlobalArgs, InitArgs, InitVersioning, OutputFormat};\nuse crate::error::CliError;\nuse crate::output::emit_report;\nuse crate::render;\nuse crate::runner::CliCommandRunner;\nuse crate::tty;\nuse crate::workspace::workspace_root;\n\npub const VERSIONING_PROMPT: &str = \"How should packages be versioned?\";\npub const SHIP_PROMPT: &str = \"Ship binaries as GitHub release assets?\";\npub const PRODUCT_PROMPT: &str = \"Which package is the product whose binaries ship?\";\npub const FORGE_PROMPT: &str = \"GitHub repository to release to (owner/repo)\";\npub const TARGETS_PROMPT: &str = \"Artifact target triples (comma-separated)\";\npub const WRITE_PROMPT: &str = \"Write callisto.toml?\";\npub const WORKFLOW_PROMPT: &str = \"Generate a GitHub Actions release workflow?\";\n/// Printed instead of the preview when the repository has no commit to plan from.\npub const NO_COMMITS: &str =\n    \"No commits yet: commit, then run `callisto release --dry-run` to preview the first release.\";\n/// Printed instead of asking `WORKFLOW_PROMPT` for a workspace no generated workflow covers.\nfn workflow_unsupported_note(reason: scaffold::WorkflowUnsupported) -> String {\n    format!(\"Skipping GitHub Actions workflow generation: {reason}.\")\n}\n/// Printed once a generated workflow is written: a merge to `branch` is the release approval.\nfn merge_publishes_note(branch: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\n        \"Merging to `{branch}` publishes: require pull requests and reviews on `{branch}` (GitHub → Settings → Rules).\"\n    )\n}\nconst VERSIONING_CHOICES: [&str; 2] = [\n    \"independent: each package has its own version\",\n    \"fixed: every package shares one version\",\n];\n\n/// Asks the operator questions; a scripted implementation drives tests.\npub trait Prompter {\n    fn select(&mut self, prompt: &str, items: &[String]) -> Result<usize, CliError>;\n    fn confirm(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: bool) -> Result<bool, CliError>;\n    fn input(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: Option<&str>) -> Result<String, CliError>;\n}\n\nstruct TerminalPrompter;\n\nimpl Prompter for TerminalPrompter {\n    fn select(&mut self, prompt: &str, items: &[String]) -> Result<usize, CliError> {\n        Ok(Select::new().with_prompt(prompt).items(items).default(0).interact()?)\n    }\n\n    fn confirm(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: bool) -> Result<bool, CliError> {\n        Ok(Confirm::new().with_prompt(prompt).default(default).interact()?)\n    }\n\n    fn input(&mut self, prompt: &str, default: Option<&str>) -> Result<String, CliError> {\n        let mut input = Input::<String>::new().with_prompt(prompt);\n        if let Some(default) = default {\n            input = input.default(default.to_owned());\n        }\n        Ok(input.interact_text()?)\n    }\n}\n\npub fn handle(args: InitArgs, global: &GlobalArgs) -> Result<ExitCode, CliError> {\n    run(\n        args,\n        global,\n        tty::is_interactive(),\n        &mut TerminalPrompter,\n        &mut std::io::stdout(),\n        &mut std::io::stderr(),\n        &CliCommandRunner,\n    )\n}\n\n/// `init` against explicit terminal state, prompter, output streams, and command runner.\npub fn run<R: CommandRunner>(\n    args: InitArgs,\n    global: &GlobalArgs,\n    interactive: bool,\n    prompter: &mut dyn Prompter,\n    out: &mut dyn Write,\n    err: &mut dyn Write,\n    runner: &R,\n) -> Result<ExitCode, CliError> {\n    validate_flags(&args)?;\n    let root = workspace_root(global, runner)?;\n    let locator = IgnoreWalkLocator::new(&root);\n    let facts = scaffold::detect(&root, &locator, runner)?;\n    let json = global.format == OutputFormat::Json;\n    // JSON keeps stdout for the report.\n    let human: &mut dyn Write = if json { &mut *err } else { &mut *out };\n    write_facts(&facts, human)?;\n\n    if facts.origin.is_none() {\n        if args.workflow {\n            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresOrigin { flag: \"workflow\" });\n        }\n        if !args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresOrigin {\n                flag: \"artifact-target\",\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    if !interactive && !args.yes {\n        let mut missing = vec![\"--yes\"];\n        missing.extend(missing_flags(&args, &facts));\n        return Err(CliError::InitRequiresYes { missing });\n    }\n    if args.yes {\n        let missing = missing_flags(&args, &facts);\n        if !missing.is_empty() {\n            return Err(CliError::InitMissingFlags { missing });\n        }\n    }\n    let prompting = interactive && !args.yes;\n    let answers = collect_answers(&args, &facts, prompting, prompter)?;\n\n    let mut diagnostics = scaffold::changesets_config_diagnostics(&facts.root);\n    if facts.origin.is_none() {\n        writeln!(human, \"{ORIGIN_MISSING_NOTE}\")?;\n        diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n            code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::InitOriginMissing,\n            severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n            message: ORIGIN_MISSING_NOTE.to_owned(),\n            package: None,\n            path: None,\n            escalated_by: None,\n            governed_by: None,\n        });\n    }\n    let shape = match scaffold::workflow_shape(&facts, &answers) {\n        Err(reason) if args.workflow => {\n            return Err(GraphError::InitWorkflowUnsupported {\n                reason: reason.to_string(),\n            }\n            .into());\n        }\n        Err(reason) => {\n            let note = workflow_unsupported_note(reason);\n            writeln!(human, \"{note}\")?;\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::WorkflowGenerationUnsupported,\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Warning,\n                message: note,\n                package: None,\n                path: None,\n                escalated_by: None,\n                governed_by: None,\n            });\n            None\n        }\n        Ok(shape) => Some(shape),\n    };\n    let want_workflow = match shape {\n        None => false,\n        Some(_) if args.workflow => true,\n        Some(_) if args.no_workflow => false,\n        Some(_) if prompting && facts.origin.is_some() => prompter.confirm(WORKFLOW_PROMPT, false)?,\n        Some(_) => false,\n    };\n    let workflow = match shape.filter(|_| want_workflow) {\n        Some(shape) => {\n            scaffold::ensure_workflow_absent(&facts.root)?;\n            let branch = scaffold::default_branch(runner, &facts.root);\n            writeln!(human, \"  default branch: {} (from {})\", branch.name, branch.source)?;\n            let version = env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\");\n            let commit = scaffold::resolve_release_commit(runner, &facts.root, version)?;\n            let content = scaffold::render_workflow(&facts, shape, &branch.name, &commit, version);\n            Some((content, branch.name))\n        }\n        None => None,\n    };\n\n    let config = scaffold::render_config(&facts, &answers);\n    let plan = if facts.has_commit {\n        Some(scaffold::preview(&facts, &config, &locator, runner)?)\n    } else {\n        None\n    };\n    writeln!(human, \"\\ncallisto.toml:\\n{config}\")?;\n    match plan {\n        Some(plan) => {\n            writeln!(human, \"First release preview (`callisto release --dry-run`):\")?;\n            super::release::write_release_preview(plan.as_ref(), OutputFormat::Text, human)?;\n        }\n        None => writeln!(human, \"{NO_COMMITS}\")?,\n    }\n    if let Some((workflow, _)) = &workflow {\n        writeln!(\n            human,\n            \"\\n{}:\\n{workflow}\",\n            scaffold::workflow_path(&facts.root).display()\n        )?;\n    }\n\n    // Computed before any write, so the `.changeset/README.md` existence check sees disk state as-is.\n    let files = scaffold::init_files(&facts.root, workflow.is_some())?;\n    let mut report = if global.dry_run {\n        InitReport {\n            schema_version: SCHEMA_VERSION,\n            initialized: false,\n            config_path: facts.root.join(\"callisto.toml\"),\n            config,\n            files,\n            diagnostics: Vec::new(),\n        }\n    } else {\n        if prompting && !prompter.confirm(WRITE_PROMPT, true)? {\n            writeln!(human, \"Initialization cancelled; nothing was written.\")?;\n            return Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS);\n        }\n        let permit = ApplyPermit::granted_unless_dry_run(global.dry_run).expect(\"non-dry-run permits writes\");\n        let mut report = scaffold::write(&facts.root, &config, &permit)?;\n        if let Some((workflow, branch)) = &workflow {\n            scaffold::write_workflow(&facts.root, workflow, &permit)?;\n            let note = merge_publishes_note(branch);\n            writeln!(human, \"{note}\")?;\n            diagnostics.push(callisto_model::Diagnostic {\n                code: callisto_model::DiagnosticCode::WorkflowMergePublishes,\n                severity: callisto_model::DiagnosticSeverity::Info,\n                message: note,\n                package: None,\n                path: None,\n                escalated_by: None,\n                governed_by: None,\n            });\n        }\n        report.files = files;\n        report\n    };\n    report.diagnostics.extend(diagnostics);\n    if json {\n        emit_report(&mut &mut *out, &report, global.dry_run)?;\n    } else {\n        render::render_init(&report, &mut &mut *out)?;\n    }\n    Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS)\n}\n\n/// Printed, and recorded as a warning diagnostic, when no `origin` remote is configured.\nconst ORIGIN_MISSING_NOTE: &str = \"No `origin` remote is configured: skipping the release workflow and \\\nshipping-binaries questions; `callisto release` will refuse until one is added.\";\n\n/// Rejects flag combinations invalid regardless of workspace facts.\nfn validate_flags(args: &InitArgs) -> Result<(), CliError> {\n    if args.workflow && args.no_workflow {\n        return Err(CliError::InitWorkflowFlagsConflict);\n    }\n    if args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n        if args.forge_repository.is_some() {\n            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresArtifactTarget {\n                flag: \"forge-repository\",\n            });\n        }\n        if args.product_package.is_some() {\n            return Err(CliError::InitFlagRequiresArtifactTarget {\n                flag: \"product-package\",\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nfn write_facts(facts: &InitFacts, out: &mut dyn Write) -> Result<(), CliError> {\n    let ecosystems: Vec<&str> = facts.ecosystems.iter().map(|ecosystem| ecosystem.prefix()).collect();\n    writeln!(out, \"Detected:\")?;\n    writeln!(out, \"  ecosystems: {}\", ecosystems.join(\", \"))?;\n    writeln!(out, \"  origin: {}\", facts.origin.as_deref().unwrap_or(\"none\"))?;\n    writeln!(out, \"  packages:\")?;\n    for package in &facts.packages {\n        let tag = package.last_tag.as_ref().map_or(\"none\", |tag| tag.as_str());\n        write!(out, \"    {} {} (last tag: {tag}\", package.id, package.version)?;\n        if package.is_binary() {\n            write!(out, \"; binary: {}\", package.bin_names.join(\", \"))?;\n        }\n        writeln!(out, \")\")?;\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// Flags `--yes` needs that were not supplied.\nfn missing_flags(args: &InitArgs, facts: &InitFacts) -> Vec<&'static str> {\n    let mut missing = Vec::new();\n    if args.versioning.is_none() {\n        missing.push(\"--versioning\");\n    }\n    if !args.artifact_targets.is_empty() && facts.binary_packages().next().is_some() {\n        if args.forge_repository.is_none() {\n            missing.push(\"--forge-repository\");\n        }\n        if args.product_package.is_none() && facts.binary_packages().nth(1).is_some() {\n            missing.push(\"--product-package\");\n        }\n    }\n    missing\n}\n\nfn missing(flag: &'static str) -> CliError {\n    CliError::InitMissingFlags { missing: vec![flag] }\n}\n\nfn collect_answers(\n    args: &InitArgs,\n    facts: &InitFacts,\n    prompting: bool,\n    prompter: &mut dyn Prompter,\n) -> Result<InitAnswers, CliError> {\n    let versioning = match args.versioning {\n        Some(InitVersioning::Fixed) => Versioning::Fixed,\n        Some(InitVersioning::Independent) => Versioning::Independent,\n        None if prompting => {\n            let choices: Vec<String> = VERSIONING_CHOICES.iter().map(|choice| (*choice).to_owned()).collect();\n            match prompter.select(VERSIONING_PROMPT, &choices)? {\n                0 => Versioning::Independent,\n                _ => Versioning::Fixed,\n            }\n        }\n        None => return Err(missing(\"--versioning\")),\n    };\n    let no_binaries = InitAnswers {\n        versioning,\n        binaries: None,\n    };\n\n    let binaries: Vec<&InitPackage> = facts.binary_packages().collect();\n    if binaries.is_empty() && !args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n        if let Some(package) = facts.unsupported_artifact_packages().next() {\n            return Err(GraphError::InitUnsupportedArtifactBuilder {\n                package: package.id.clone(),\n                ecosystem: package\n                    .id\n                    .split_once('/')\n                    .map_or(\"unknown\", |(ecosystem, _)| ecosystem)\n                    .to_owned(),\n            }\n            .into());\n        }\n        return Err(GraphError::InitNoBinaryPackage.into());\n    }\n    let requested_product = args\n        .product_package\n        .as_deref()\n        .map(|name| facts.product_package(name))\n        .transpose()?;\n    if binaries.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(no_binaries);\n    }\n    // No `origin`: the forge question below has nothing to validate a repository against, so\n    // shipping is never offered (skips straight to `no_binaries`); `--artifact-target` without\n    // `origin` is already rejected up front in `run`.\n    let ship = !args.artifact_targets.is_empty()\n        || (facts.origin.is_some() && prompting && prompter.confirm(SHIP_PROMPT, false)?);\n    if !ship {\n        return Ok(no_binaries);\n    }\n\n    let product = match (requested_product, binaries.as_slice()) {\n        (Some(product), _) => product,\n        (None, [only]) => only,\n        (None, _) if prompting => {\n            let ids: Vec<String> = binaries.iter().map(|package| package.id.clone()).collect();\n            binaries[prompter.select(PRODUCT_PROMPT, &ids)?]\n        }\n        (None, _) => return Err(missing(\"--product-package\")),\n    };\n\n    let forge_repository = match &args.forge_repository {\n        Some(value) => scaffold::forge_repository(facts, value)?,\n        None if prompting => {\n            let detected = facts.origin_repository.as_ref().map(|repository| repository.as_slug());\n            scaffold::forge_repository(facts, &prompter.input(FORGE_PROMPT, detected.as_deref())?)?\n        }\n        None => return Err(missing(\"--forge-repository\")),\n    };\n\n    let targets = if args.artifact_targets.is_empty() {\n        loop {\n            let answer = prompter.input(TARGETS_PROMPT, None)?;\n            let targets: Vec<String> = answer.split(',').map(str::trim).map(str::to_owned).collect();\n            if targets.iter().all(|target| target.is_empty()) {\n                // Nothing meaningful submitted: re-ask rather than error.\n                continue;\n            }\n            break targets;\n        }\n    } else {\n        args.artifact_targets.clone()\n    };\n    let targets = scaffold::validate_targets(&targets)?;\n\n    Ok(InitAnswers {\n        versioning,\n        binaries: Some(BinaryRelease {\n            product: product.id.clone(),\n            forge_repository,\n            targets,\n        }),\n    })\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests;\n","numLines":414,"startLine":1,"totalLines":414}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"83cd3dd7-83a9-494c-bffa-d11f6fc4d59a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/init-defaults","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
